Probe: scratch test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/probe/probe_test.go, overlaid as internal/config/profile/probe_scratch_test.go. Command: `CGO_ENABLED=0 go test -count=1 -overlay .../probe/overlay.json -run TestProbeUntabSeparators -v ./internal/config/profile/`. It calls public Parse with Options{} and parseWith at splitAt -1, 0 and 1. Output (every split matches the public result):
- "k: a\"\t:b\n" => {k@1:1:s:"a\" :b"@1:4}
- "k: x'\t:y z\n" => {k@1:1:s:"x' :y z"@1:4}
- "k: [a\"\t:b]\n" => {k@1:1:[s:"a\" :b"@1:5]}
- "k: {\"a\":a\"\t:aa:ba\"}\n" => {k@1:1:{a@1:5:s:"a\" :aa:ba\""@1:9}}
- "a\"\t:b: 1\na\" :b: 2\n" => RZ-CFG-002@2:1 (false duplicate key)
- "a\"\t:b: 1\n" => {a" :b@1:1:i:1@1:8} (key changed)
- control "k: a\t:b\n" => {k@1:1:s:"a\t:b"@1:4} (correct when no quote character comes before the tab)
Reference: yaml.v3 v3.0.1 from the module cache, in a scratch module outside the repo, run with the repo's go1.27.1 toolchain binary:
- "k: a\"\t:b\n" => {"k":"a\"\t:b"}
- "k: x'\t:y z\n" => {"k":"x'\t:y z"}
- "k: [a\"\t:b]\n" => ["a\"\t:b"]
- "k: {\"a\":a\"\t:aa:ba\"}\n" => {"a":"a\"\t:aa:ba\""}
- "a\"\t:b: 1\na\" :b: 2\n" => two keys, {"a\"\t:b":1, "a\" :b":2}, no error.
No repository file was created or changed: the probe went in through -overlay, and `ls internal/config/profile | grep probe` finds nothing.

